      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So you're saying the demographic details and clothing are essentially acting as proxies for their character in the eyes of a jury. Following that logic, if the roles were reversed—say, the witness in the suit was a young Hispanic man in a hoodie and the witness in the hoodie was an older Caucasian man in professional attire—would the assessment of their \"reliability\" change entirely? Like, would the hoodie and age automatically make the testimony less credible regardless of what was actually said?",
